compat exit 132
Additional check (2026-10-26): an alternative digiemu venv contains a different
build (806512 bytes, sha256 a0db6bebc7506245be341971a4b7a67d012aa37ee3e46ebc39679b88137e503f),
but it also aborts with SIGILL (status 132) at uc_mem_map:
  unicorn/unicorn_py3/unicorn.py:831 in mem_map
The other two venvs have a 16,232,448-byte library
(sha256 7207c8e3d7a63118fb0bca73e01816797fd51b1d8a39a4cbc7abfd562ee59c85) with
the same mem_map SIGILL. A bare Uc(UC_ARCH_M68K, UC_MODE_BIG_ENDIAN).mem_map(0, 0x1000)
reproduces it, so this is a runtime/ABI failure before any guest instruction.
The 806 KB library's strings name a local digitakt2-unicorn build tree; it is
still not usable by this emulator on this host.


Root cause and host workaround (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------------------
The machine's sysctlbyname("hw.cachelinesize") is denied with EPERM in this
execution environment. Unicorn's init_cache_info falls back to `mrs CTR_EL0`
when that sysctl fails; on this host a bare `mrs CTR_EL0` traps with SIGILL.
That is why every candidate library failed before loading firmware.

A host-only copy of the alternative library was made under /tmp and its
fallback `mrs CTR_EL0` was replaced with a fixed cache-line-size value
(128 bytes). With PYTHONPATH pointing at that copy:
  emu.unicorn_compat -> all five checks pass.
A clean stock 1.53 bootstrap then reached:
  ladder: parked at ~160M instructions, 10 tasks
  intro: USER INTERFACE IS LIVE
  settle: SETTLED at 750M, accepted; gui.snap saved.
This is a local workaround, not a tracked patch. Run outside this sandbox
(where hw.cachelinesize works) or build the real patched Unicorn instead.
